    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "CUSTOM EVENTS\n\nA custom event is your own entry point with typed parameters, like a function that other parts of\nthe graph (or other objects) can call. Define it in the Events panel: name Greet, fields name (String)\nand times (i64). Two nodes appear: the red 'On Greet' event (the handler, with the fields as output\npins) and the 'Greet' dispatch node you place wherever you want to fire it.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "FIRING THE EVENT\nBegin Play dispatches Greet twice with different parameters (typed on the node). A dispatch runs the handler immediately and then continues with the next node, so the output reads: Ada x2, then Linus x1.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -70.0
        ],
        "size": [
          960.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "d1",
          "d2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "THE HANDLER\nOn Greet starts a new chain whenever the event fires. Its 'name' and 'times' pins hold the values the caller passed: times drives a For Loop, name is joined into the message, and a counter records every greeting (3 in total).",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          440.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1260.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.55,
          0.15,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "on",
          "loop",
          "hello",
          "say",
          "gg",
          "g1",
          "sg"
        ]
      }
    ],
